<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<section xml:id="expansions-unlike-factors">
  <title>Verticals and Wings: Unlike Factors</title>
  <p>Arrange the two binomials vertically. The first product <m>(3x)(2y)=6xy</m> and the last product <m>(-7)(9)=-63</m> go straight down. The cross-products travel to the wings: <m>(-7)(2y)=-14y</m> at the left and <m>(3x)(9)=27x</m> at the right. Keep all four terms when they are unlike.</p><p>Draw arrows to visualise the four products while learning. You may leave the arrows out of your own calculations when you can confidently picture those routes.</p>
  <me>(3x-7)(2y+9)=-14y+6xy-63+27x.</me>
  <figure xml:id="falling-fan-figure">
    <caption>The completed worked example and the unnumbered questions, arranged as on the classroom sheet.</caption>
    <interactive xml:id="falling-fan-interactive" iframe="https://ronandownes.github.io/maths/apps/falling-fan/index.html" width="100%" aspect="16:9"/>
  </figure>
  <p><url href="https://ronandownes.github.io/maths/apps/falling-fan/index.html" visual="Open the complete interactive sheet full screen"/> to see the paths clearly, hide or show the arrows, print the page or reveal answers when checking your work.</p>
  <paragraphs xml:id="expansions-unlike-factors-print">
    <title>Print-friendly mathematical layout</title>
    <p>The six stacks are reproduced here for print and for use when an embedded page is unavailable. The completed calculation is shown above; the remaining calculations are unnumbered.</p>
    <me>\begin{array}{ccc}
\begin{array}{r}3x-7\\[3pt]2y+9\\[-2pt]\hline\end{array}
&amp;\qquad\begin{array}{r}7+2m\\[3pt]3n+5\\[-2pt]\hline\end{array}
&amp;\qquad\begin{array}{r}3a^2+2\\[3pt]5b^2+7\\[-2pt]\hline\end{array}\\[3.5em]
\begin{array}{r}2r+7\\[3pt]5+2t\\[-2pt]\hline\end{array}
&amp;\qquad\begin{array}{r}2u+1\\[3pt]5v+3\\[-2pt]\hline\end{array}
&amp;\qquad\begin{array}{r}5e+F\\[3pt]F^2+3\\[-2pt]\hline\end{array}
\end{array}</me>
  </paragraphs>
</section>
